values ('d2e3f4a5-6b7c-4d92-9e12-2f3a4b5c6d32', 'asian-history', 'Asian History', 'Asian History is an advanced undergraduate course that introduces students to the major political, social, cultural, religious, economic, imperial, and environmental histories of Asia from ancient foundations to the present. The course treats Asia as a connected but internally diverse field, integrating East Asia, South Asia, Southeast Asia, Central and Inner Asia, and Islamic and Indian Ocean worlds. Students work with primary sources, material culture, maps, visual evidence, historiography, and digital archives while building a final source-based historical argument.');

